{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Have I not been accustomed to you?</b> As the Targum renders it; and so ״הַלְאֵל יִסְכָּן גָּבֶר״ (Job 22). And our Sages expounded this verse in the Talmud — they said to him: What is the reason you did not ride a mule? He said to them: I sent him out to graze, etc. — as is found in tractate Avodah Zarah (page 4)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "the Aramaic-style words בִּרְטִיבָא שְׁדַאי לֵיהּ כו' ('I sent him out to pasture, etc.') are left untranslated as Rashi cites them verbatim from the Talmudic passage (Avodah Zarah 4b) without translating them into Hebrew"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:17.316969490Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}